[{"name":"AdamMil/GPGDesktop","owner":"AdamMil","html_url":"https://github.com/AdamMil/GPGDesktop","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"This is an attempt to make encryption simpler to use for the average person by providing a front end to the GNU Privacy Guard. The front end is built on top of my OpenPGP security and UI libraries. It provides a powerful key manager, and wizards to walk the user through basic tasks, such as encryption, signing, decryption, and signature verification. ","topics":["decryption","encryption","frontend","gpg"],"score":2213,"global_rank":221706},{"name":"AdamMil/GeneHackman","owner":"AdamMil","html_url":"https://github.com/AdamMil/GeneHackman","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":1,"language":"C#","description":"Gene Hackman is a framework for genetic programming. A novel feature is that it supports an ongoing tournament mode, where programs compete in real time rather than well-defined and distinct generations. This lends itself to certain problems well, such as those where programs can interact with each other. It also supports parallelizing the simulation across multiple threads and compiling it to native code, among other things. It might be in a somewhat broken state due to an unfinished overhaul in which I was going to add support for dynamic functions, variables, and constants.","topics":["artificial-life","genetic-algorithm","genetic-programming"],"score":2213,"global_rank":221707},{"name":"AdamMil/Chrono","owner":"AdamMil","html_url":"https://github.com/AdamMil/Chrono","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"An incomplete reimplementation of a nifty roguelike for .NET. Some of the data files may have been lost.","topics":["roguelike","roguelike-game"],"score":2213,"global_rank":221708},{"name":"traies/TP4-Horror","owner":"traies","html_url":"https://github.com/traies/TP4-Horror","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":n